    sections: [{"h2": "Do small businesses still need a VPN?", "paras": ["Traditional VPNs connect remote staff into the office network. Many small businesses now run almost entirely on cloud apps, so the question is less about 'a VPN' and more about secure remote access: who can reach which apps, from which devices.", "That is why business VPNs and zero-trust network access (ZTNA) services are now often compared side by side."]}, {"h2": "Business VPN vs consumer VPN", "paras": ["Consumer VPNs are built for individual privacy. Business VPNs add central management: user provisioning, dedicated or static IPs, access policies, audit logs and integration with identity providers. Many consumer VPN terms also restrict commercial use."]}, {"h2": "NordLayer", "paras": ["NordLayer, from the company behind NordVPN, is designed for small and mid-sized teams. It offers central admin, shared and dedicated gateways, and identity-provider integration, with a setup that does not need a network engineer. Check current plans and per-user pricing on its site."]}, {"h2": "Perimeter 81 (now Check Point)", "paras": ["Perimeter 81 was acquired by Check Point and its service is now offered as part of Check Point's SASE portfolio. It combines VPN-style access with zero-trust features. If you are comparing it, look at the current Check Point offering rather than older reviews of the standalone product."]}, {"h2": "Cloudflare Zero Trust", "paras": ["Cloudflare Zero Trust replaces the traditional VPN with per-app access policies, DNS filtering and a lightweight device client. It has a free plan for small teams (up to 50 users at the time of writing), which makes it an easy place to start for budget-conscious businesses."]}, {"h2": "How to choose", "paras": ["Match the tool to how you work."], "list": ["Mostly cloud apps, small budget: start with Cloudflare Zero Trust", "Need dedicated IPs to allowlist in client systems: NordLayer or similar", "Already in a larger security vendor ecosystem: look at Check Point's SASE", "Need to reach on-premise servers: make sure private network access is supported", "Always require MFA and connect it to your identity provider"]}],
    title: "Best VPNs for Small Business 2026: NordLayer vs Perimeter 81 vs Cloudflare Zero Trust",
